<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The experiments are typically conducted using a forzen WavLM large model with transformer layer index <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=1,2,...,L,\quad L=12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=1,2,...,L,\quad L=12</annotation></semantics></math>, with varying the expert rank <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of MoLEx modules <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the top-<math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> expert selection out of total <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> experts. We also assess the impact of including the orthogonality regularization loss <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{orth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>orth</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{orth}}</annotation></semantics></math> alongside the cross-entropy loss <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{ce}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ce</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{ce}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Baseline comparisons include: 1) standard WavLM large model without MoLEx, with 12-layer and 24-layer variants; 2) WavLM large model with sigle expert for each transformer, assessing performance without mixture-based selection.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T4.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">TABLE IV</span>: </span><span id="S4.T4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Performance from other single models on ASVSpoof 5 evaluation Track 1. (finetuned-FT; data augmented-DA)</span></figcaption>
<table id="S4.T4.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T4.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T4.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_ttt" style="padding-left:1.7pt;padding-right:1.7pt;" colspan="2"><span id="S4.T4.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Model name</span></th>
<th id="S4.T4.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_ttt" style="padding-left:1.7pt;padding-right:1.7pt;" colspan="2"><span id="S4.T4.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">EER (%)</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
